    "body": "Yes. I think we're in general in trouble though for the default type... e.g. it should apply to `<input type=\"asedfsdfdfdf\">` too, right? Seems like CSS just isn't capable of solving this yet...\n\nOr, I guess we could just do `input:not(... match everything but text/search/tel/url/email ...)`? A pretty bad hack.\n",
